      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I apologize for the detour into the clinical jungle. Let's get back to the billing jungle, shall we?\n\nI understand your concern about capturing the chaotic and hypertrophic nature of the growth. It's a bit like trying to describe a goblin's lair to a skeptical goblin-hunter – you need to use vivid language to convey the complexity of the morphology.\n\nIn this case, you might consider using the \"unspecified\" code (L71.9) as a starting point, but with a detailed description of the morphology that highlights its unique features. For example, you could use the following modifiers to add specificity:\n\n* L71.9, with a modifier of \"multiple, irregular, and hypertrophic epidermal growths\" to convey the chaotic and disorganized nature of the clusters.\n* L71.9, with a modifier of \"with crusting, scaling, and ulceration\" to highlight the aggressive and hypertrophic features of the growths.\n\nAlternatively, you could consider using the \"unspecified\" code (L71.9) and then adding a detailed description of the morphology in the clinical notes or in a separate addendum. This can help to provide additional context and support for the claim, which may",
      "source": "target",
